{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_35c1086f7984478f9d3976eac4294ddf","id":"pg_3eb2d6ce1d595803ba2f97c6e502b47e","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/atomgit-atomcode-atomcode-context-md-287bff70f940-97c6e502b47e.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_d2a4dd1e1a4b58d3b49ca8e411259931"],"title":"atomgit-atomcode/atomcode/CONTEXT.md @ 287bff70f940","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_35c1086f7984478f9d3976eac4294ddf"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_00eae0f8d64346c3586edbbd51f6a00d1cbc755d551d5bf6c936f0f1a85f5e67"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A .atomcode.md file in the project root provides persistent context included in the system prompt; AGENTS.md is supported as an alternative, with .atomcode.md taking priority if both exist."},{"claim_ids":["clm_089ea0040d451ad7b64b7381919c204da583f0ac7cd08ad10e4aa561b7ccc679"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent loop features autonomous multi-step execution, a verification loop with syntax checks, a dynamic step budget scaled to edited files, loop detection, and 3-layer JSON repair of malformed tool-call arguments."},{"claim_ids":["clm_08c31351ad595ea9812a87d8ab50015879184bc417cb36adf2573a5e23c540e3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Built-in tools include file/shell operations (read_file, edit_file, bash, grep, glob), web search/fetch, code-graph tools (list_symbols, trace_callers, blast_radius), auto_fix, and use_skill."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0e6f1f7b99ed565085621d43ee3cbec4a7787efef7ea919cb62736264e85c814"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"AtomCode is described as an open-source terminal AI coding agent written in Rust, positioned as an alternative to Claude Code / Cursor Agent that connects to any OpenAI-compatible API."},{"claim_ids":["clm_35a5d6b1d650ac960ce1cf0ccd0f2fc1cdd81f09323db43c9397ec65b3bff83c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A /webui command launches a local browser UI bound to 127.0.0.1 with a one-time token; /app enables mobile remote access via a reverse WSS relay with QR-code pairing and bidirectional sync."},{"claim_ids":["clm_49d2c60655195a255a1ce915e76e746cd8783da3252247fb5a34028793dd123a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The turn-level datalog is described as supporting replay, debugging, and eval harnesses, suggesting the product provides structured logs intended for evaluation use."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4c6a0c1bea34b440959609435f47c8abed84054eabd139cfcc40a67b541406a8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration lives at ~/.atomcode/config.toml with provider entries (type, api_key, model, base_url, context_window); /reload picks up manual edits without restart, and a first-run wizard guides provider setup."},{"claim_ids":["clm_54c6366498d4def7fc5f511f2a3b68c42018d63c87ebbe846a2c0a6c00ba7447"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent supports multiple LLM providers via OpenAI function-calling, including Claude, OpenAI, DeepSeek, Zhipu GLM, Qwen, SiliconFlow, Ollama (partial), and any OpenAI-compatible API."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5fc56691298269bc57cecbf43633e8f69fcf3e71c305c46b4d22e528a66b86e5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers persistent sessions (--continue, /resume), AtomGit OAuth login, SSO login, headless single-prompt mode, and a daemon exposing an HTTP API with SSE streaming chat."},{"claim_ids":["clm_73275af1f59ee353b86e494a61583791cf7002e146f64847455c3ceedbb979c6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Building from source requires Rust 1.88+ because older Cargo versions cannot parse the current lockfile; runtime needs an API key from a supported provider or an AtomGit account."},{"claim_ids":["clm_822c8dcc69e6e583f4941aebb04e369e0886e984599898196fe24568d054d1a2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users can define custom slash commands as Markdown template files with frontmatter (name, description, args) in global, project-level, or plugin directories; project-level overrides global, but custom commands cannot shadow built-ins."},{"claim_ids":["clm_86e0faadae3537376403d61d2793ffd32125a2e291fdc90b687ff778a07a0c3a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In headless mode (-p), approval-required bash calls are auto-approved and logged to stderr, while other approval-required tools are denied."},{"claim_ids":["clm_95b05bd687c241cc3ac3f4af54bdbb6c3b3a99a26c4a06463a4db33341fb6ee8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CodingPlan request signer is closed-source and only present in official builds; self-built binaries cannot sign requests, so /login cannot claim free CodingPlan models, though own API providers work without it."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a290eae041ada055a8661e1e3c8b31a04d326d6fadf1c1abbf59dbf64674f743"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Memory commands let users save facts (/remember, with --global scope), remove them (/forget), and list them (/memory); sessions are persisted and resumable."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b95e15240a16ea0435d682f5db24433bfad078e95fafadb3ead3e660a1940b78"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Stated design principles include tech-stack agnosticism via descriptor-file detection (package.json, Cargo.toml, etc.), a single CodingRuntime owner, tool safety, token-budget-aware context windowing, and directed dependencies keeping the kernel neutral."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cbb2323c20895ee52d28a26ff0e6c7412e53764d3d22d8632c31e65f8bee8c3c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is a layered Rust workspace with crates for kernel (agent loop), capabilities (providers/tools/MCP/skills/sessions/memory), coding, review, TUI, CLI, and daemon (HTTP/SSE/WebSocket transport)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e7550ac01d291827ea20791a91618b2bc81ae16ada5c0e65273d16d1ade99b36"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: building from source requires Rust 1.88+ and Git; the webui frontend must be built with npm before the Rust build (webui/dist is gitignored and embedded), and cargo clean -p atomcode-daemon is needed after frontend rebuilds."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ee22d46a1d91999e100a62ef57f57d410edd1e14a9ba9a13aaac86a62f24acf8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Destructive commands (rm -rf, git push --force, DROP TABLE) require explicit approval; writes outside the workspace, sensitive paths, and source-file deletion get stronger confirmation rules, with per-session grants and /undo rollback."}],"claim_ids":["clm_00eae0f8d64346c3586edbbd51f6a00d1cbc755d551d5bf6c936f0f1a85f5e67","clm_089ea0040d451ad7b64b7381919c204da583f0ac7cd08ad10e4aa561b7ccc679","clm_08c31351ad595ea9812a87d8ab50015879184